 [{:id :s1a-protocol/deadline-excludes-blocking-parent-validation
   :disposition :confirmed :priority :P1 :confidence 1.0
   :code [{:file "src/oikos/infra/bb_render.cljs" :lines [65 71] :reason "Same-event-loop timer is cleared when finish! publishes the result."}
          {:file "src/oikos/infra/bb_render.cljs" :lines [112 126] :reason "The close handler synchronously validates acceptance and commits completion without comparing elapsed time to a deadline."}
          {:file "src/oikos/law/generation.cljc" :lines [265 279] :reason "Acceptance synchronously revalidates the request, parses the frame and validates every artifact."}]
   :frozen-contract [{:file "docs/specs/s1a-generation-contracts.md" :lines [313 319] :requirement "5000 ms wall deadline measured from spawn; validate every artifact before acceptance."}
                     {:file "docs/specs/s1a-generation-contracts.md" :lines [329 335] :requirement "No late callback publishes artifacts; deadline yields a terminal Result by 6000 ms including cleanup."}]
   :reproduction
   {:saved-probe :deadline-bb-echo
    :saved-source-lines [153 163]
    :payload "f/payload with TEST_TOKEN plus 128 synthetic ENV_<i>_<88 A characters> available-env names; 32 dev config targets named target-0 through target-31."
    :request-id "validation-deadline"
    :payload-sha "ad97f7cde1c24e5be2fd0770472131b288ec013073410ebb036017b631878d9e"
    :child "Actual BB reads at most 1048577 stdin bytes and immediately writes/flushes those exact bytes to stdout. Feed the precomputed valid response through the test-owned stdin substitution."
    :acceptance "Unmodified adapter request checks, streamed caps, close handling and full g/accept-response execute against the valid response."
    :measurement "performance.now timestamps immediately after original spawn returns, in the independently registered close observer, and at Promise settlement. Pre-spawn request/render computation is excluded. Stamping after spawn return conservatively undercounts elapsed time."}
   :observed
   {:request-utf8-bytes 19930 :request-cap 262144
    :response-utf8-bytes 440243 :stdout-observed-bytes 440243 :stdout-cap 1048576
    :targets 32 :target-cap 64
    :spawn-to-close-ms 11.992944999999963
    :spawn-to-settle-ms 11630.367805999998
    :close-to-settle-ms 11618.374861
    :status :ok :code nil :close-ack true :cleanup-holds []}
   :counterargument "A slow real renderer may correctly time out; perhaps the observed delay is pre-spawn preparation or an unrelated S1B effect-edge obligation."
   :resolution "The fresh measurement excludes all preparation and starts at actual spawn. The real BB child closes after about 12 ms, yet unmodified parent verification returns :ok after about 11.63 s. The 5 s acceptance deadline and 6 s terminal bound are S1A's own frozen process contract, independently of S1B or writes. One observed late :ok is sufficient; no exhaustive schedule claim is needed."
   :repair-direction "Do not rely solely on a timer on the validation event loop. Keep parent verification interruptible/off-thread or prove/enforce a bounded work budget, and recheck a monotonic deadline before publishing success. A final elapsed-time check alone prevents late :ok but does not restore the six-second terminal bound."
   :regression-direction
   {:test "Real fast BB below-cap 32-target echo using this exact fixture; measure from actual spawn, not start! entry."
    :assert "No :ok after 5000 ms; terminal Result by 6000 ms including verification and cleanup; no accepted artifacts after timeout. Retain close/cleanup observations."
    :deterministic-addition "Exercise deadline expiry while parent acceptance is pending and before success publication, with an independently progressing clock/interruptible verifier. Never treat a child-sleep timeout test or post-hoc late error as proof of the full terminal bound."
    :limit "This skeptic ran one fresh real-BB schedule, not exhaustive timing/cancellation enumeration. Absolute durations are host-dependent, while the measured breach and causal blocking path are direct observations."}}
  {:id :s1a-protocol/textdecoder-erases-bom-bytes
